    {
      "key": "Classical logic has a rule",
      "order": 6,
      "act": "Act IV",
      "truth": "Classical logic has a rule: if a contradiction exists, everything follows. One false step and the entire system collapses into triviality. Pavel Florensky — mathematician, priest, executed by Stalin — rejected this.",
